[h1]Bug Reports[/h1]
Post bugs in this thread only. One bug per reply, so each can be tracked and answered. Questions and suggestions belong in their own threads.

[h2]Before you post[/h2]
[olist]
    [*]Confirm Harmony, ButterLib, and Mod Configuration Menu (MCM) are enabled in the launcher, below them in load order.
    [*]Confirm you are on Bannerlord v1.3.15 through v1.5.2. This release supports that whole span, and every download reaches all of it.
    [*]Check whether the bug still happens with every other mod disabled. If it goes away, say which mod brings it back.
    [*]If the issue is about character creation content (wrong starting gear, a missing chapter, and so on), say which route you took, which of the eight starts you began as, and whether Story Mode was on. On Cultured Start the start is named for you on the screen that reads your life back.
[/olist]

[h2]The log[/h2]
Cultured Start Reloaded logs through ButterLib, with a file fallback at:
[code]Documents\Mount and Blade II Bannerlord\Configs\ModLogs\CulturedStartReloaded<date>.log[/code]
Copy the file from right after the bug happens. Steam comments strip long pastes, so upload the whole file to a paste site or file host and link it rather than pasting only the lines you think matter.

[h2]What to include[/h2]
Copy this template into your reply and fill in every line:
[code]
Mod version:        (the version shown on this Workshop page, or the .csproj version if you know it)
Bannerlord version: (shown in the launcher)
Route:              (Cultured Start / Start Editor / Vanilla Start)
Start:              (Commoner / Mercenary / Landless Vassal / Landed Vassal / Monarch / Outlaw / Caravan Master / Rebel Clan)
Story Mode:         (on or off)
Other mods:         (the full list, or "none")
What I did:
What happened:
What I expected:
Log:                (link to the file, see above)
[/code]

[h2]What happens next[/h2]
Confirmed bugs are fixed in a PATCH update, listed in the Change Notes tab. A reply in this thread will say which version carries the fix. Reports missing the log or the version are answered with a request for them before anything else.

[h2]Not bugs[/h2]
[list]
    [*]The mod has no effect on a campaign already in progress. It only runs during character creation on a new campaign; this is by design, not a bug.
    [*]A start type is missing from the Start Editor's list because it was turned off in MCM. Every start type can be disabled individually; turning every one off brings them all back, since a start has to exist.
    [*]Cultured Start has no list of start types to pick from. Your answers decide what you begin as, and the screen after the scenes names it before anything is applied. If your life earned a start you have switched off in MCM, that screen says so and names the nearest one still open.
    [*]The seafaring content appears only when War Sails is installed: one scene becomes a waterfront, and a chapter offers three beginnings at sea. Without the DLC that scene is a town instead, the sea chapter is simply not there, and nothing else about the story changes. War Sails items are offered in the gear pickers when the DLC is installed, and its three naval skills are editable in the Start Editor.
    [*]A chapter of the guided start never appeared. Thirty-one switches under Creation Menus in MCM turn chapters and life scenes off, and a chapter is also absent when your start type, your life or a missing DLC gives it nothing to ask about.
[/list]
